nversion gates, not permission to invent parity.\\n\\n## 1. Conformance, language, and scope\\n\\n### 1.1 Normative language\\n\\nThe key words MUST, MUST NOT, REQUIRED, SHALL, SHALL NOT, SHOULD, SHOULD NOT,\\nRECOMMENDED, NOT RECOMMENDED, MAY, and OPTIONAL are to be interpreted as\\nnormative requirements when, and only when, they appear in uppercase.\\n\\nA conforming implementation MUST satisfy every MUST and MUST NOT applicable to\\nits declared conformance targets. A deviation MAY exist only behind an\\nexperimental feature gate that is disabled by default, is reported by\\n<code>ax doctor</code>, and is never advertised as an available capability.\\n\\n### 1.2 Product boundary\\n\\n<code>ax</code> manages durable coding-agent sessions across an explicitly\\ntrusted, allowlisted mesh of computers. It MUST let an operator:\\n\\n1. launch a direct provider session or a task-board-managed session;\\n2. keep the terminal durable across a local terminal disconnect and, where the\\n   terminal backend supports it, a reboot;\\n3. list ownership and replica state across the mesh;\\n4. synchronize immutable session metadata, provider state, task-board state,\\n   and the workspace state required to resume;\\n5. attach to the current owner without changing ownership;\\n6. transfer ownership gracefully or, as an explicit recovery action, forcibly;\\n7. fork from a checkpoint into a new logical session and workspace identity;\\n8. stop a session without deleting its durable state; and\\n9. resume a stopped session on its owner host;\\n10. clone durable session evidence across supported native environments into a\\n    new logical Session and independently validated native target identity;\\n11. discover managed and unmanaged Claude Code and Codex native sessions on the\\n    local and allowlisted mesh hosts without importing their transcripts into a\\n    central index;\\n12. browse sanitized, provenance-bearing directory metadata through a terminal\\n    TUI, human CLI, and typed query surface; and\\n13. produce and execute an exact, expiring Continuation Plan through existing\\n    AX ownership, workspace, transfer, materialization, cloning, and terminal\\n    authority.\\n\\nThe specified v0.5.0 product is a Go CLI, optional per-user background service, provider\\nplugin host, terminal supervisor, SSH RPC client/server, and Go-native\\n===MAIN-SPECPIN-DIFF===\\n .spec/README.md                                    |    29 -\\n .../.activity/EPIC-260829-dz9yvx/events.ndjson     |    11 +\\n .../.activity/EPIC-260830-1uwj54/events.ndjson     |   201 +\\n .../.activity/STORY-260908-18woqo/events.ndjson    |    53 +\\n .../.activity/STORY-260909-2uobs6/events.ndjson    |    26 +\\n .../.activity/TASK-260908-2tkufa/events.ndjson     |   280 +\\n .../.activity/TASK-260908-3kvnm2/events.ndjson     |   118 +\\n .../.activity/TASK-260908-eea478/events.ndjson     |     9 +\\n .../.activity/TASK-260909-3kvql5/events.ndjson     |   191 +\\n ...830-1uwj54_RUN-260907-ad43c8-blocked-audit-2.md |     1 +\\n ...830-1uwj54_RUN-260907-ad43c8-blocked-audit-3.md |     1 +\\n ...260830-1uwj54_RUN-260907-ad43c8-continuation.md |    30 +\\n ...EPIC-260830-1uwj54_RUN-260907-ad43c8-routing.md |     1 +\\n ...830-1uwj54_RUN-260908-0dbb0d-blocked-audit-2.md |     9 +\\n ...830-1uwj54_RUN-260908-0dbb0d-blocked-audit-3.md |    22 +\\n ...IC-260830-1uwj54_RUN-260908-0dbb0d-stop-line.md |    72 +\\n ...IC-260830-1uwj54_RUN-260908-6cfae8-stop-line.md |    58 +\\n ...30-1uwj54_approved-contract-execution-260908.md |     1 +\\n ...60830-1uwj54_approved-contract-resume-260908.md |    17 +\\n ...C-260830-1uwj54_orchestration-handoff-260908.md |    29 +\\n ...EPIC-260830-1uwj54_primary-blocked-audit-3.json |    23 +\\n ...C-260830-1uwj54_primary-owner-recovery-audit.md |     3 +\\n .../EPIC-260830-1uwj54_runtime-install.tar.gz      |   Bin 0 -> 2116 bytes\\n .../EPIC-260830-1uwj54_source-ci-0137.json         |   190 +\\n .../EPIC-260830-1uwj54_source-ci-followup.md       |     1 +\\n .../EPIC-260830-1uwj54_source-landing-audit.md     |    11 +\\n ...yst--orchestrator--codex-_RUN-260907-ad43c8.log |    20 +\\n ...yst--orchestrator--codex-_RUN-260908-0dbb0d.log |    21 +\\n ...yst--orchestrator--codex-_RUN-260908-6cfae8.log |     0\\n ...60908-2tkufa_change-request_rev1-validation.log |   849 +\\n .../TASK-260908-2tkufa_change-request_rev1.patch   | 24819 ++++++++++++++++++\\n ...60908-2tkufa_change-request_rev2-validation.log |   640 +\\n .../TASK-260908-2tkufa_change-request_rev2.patch   | 25070 +++++++++++++++++++\\n ...8-2tkufa_control-config-review-restoration.json |     5 +\\n .../TASK-260908-2tkufa_evidence.tar.gz             |   Bin 0 -> 561048 bytes\\n .../TASK-260908-2tkufa_integration-outcome.md      |    93 +\\n .../TASK-260908-2tkufa_ownership.md                |    52 +\\n .../TASK-260908-2tkufa_primary-implementation.md   |    11 +\\n .../TASK-260908-2tkufa_primary-integration.md      |    13 +\\n .../TASK-260908-2tkufa_primary-recovery.md         |    11 +\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5630,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1408,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
