{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000f7bb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a088d0-e609-7bb2-8da2-c35b2ea0a045"},"sequence":6712,"recorded_at":1780531400013419,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f897871b-85d1-4704-870d-e5ea0ee901cf","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f897871b-85d1-4704-870d-e5ea0ee901cf","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f897871b-85d1-4704-870d-e5ea0ee901cf"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a088f5-d729-7512-b427-3f24daf73641"},"task_id":"01a088f5-d729-7512-b427-3f24daf73641","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a088f5-d729-7512-b427-3f24daf73641","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-132-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -n 20 LOGBOOK.md 2>&1\",\n  \"description\": \"Read logbook head\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-08\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2u34k1 — configured peer identity and honest SSH authority\\n\\n- SCOPE: read-only host/peer identity in STORY-260830-1kiyj6, pinned AX v0.5.0 §§6, 11.1, 16.1. Canonical config/scalar/SSH owners are reused. Duplicate peer identity includes reuse of the local host ID; aliases remain exact, and ID/alias collisions refuse ambiguous resolution.\\n- AUTHORITY: §11.1 leaves host-key and user authentication to external SSH. No AX key-provenance TOML member, private-key reader, caller-minted verification flag, live connection, discovery authorization, or at-rest encryption claim was added. The returned SSH target and policy are configuration inputs, not authentication or payload-validation evidence.\\n- NEGATIVE EVIDENCE: first narrowing run exposed a weak raw-class test: local_only default refused export even after the class registry admitted raw_excerpts. Added a permissive-default negative; the same compiling plant now fails TestDisclosurePolicyRefusals. The grammar-only protocol-ID mutant survives because exact equality to an already-validated configured UUID still refuses it; its scope is explicitly reported, not counted as a kill.\\n- VALIDATION DISCIPLINE: an initial full test run overlapped the ownership-registry update and failed tracecheck with the old compiled digest against the new file. That run is reported exit 1; the next run exposed a missed tracecheck output-count fixture (98 instead of 105), which was corrected. Stable-tree reruns own handoff evidence. Original files remain untouched during mutants (Go overlays), with a green neutral and compiling known-bad control.\\n- BOARD: task-board validate exited 0 while reporting 225 shared activity/mirror issues; none named this leaf or its Story. The exit status is recorded, but it is not represented as an issue-free board. Shared board repair is outside this leaf.\\n- BOUNDS: no durable mutation, hence no crash-write injection. Read failure/absence/recovery and immutable snapshots are driven through Load. Sibling transport/lifecycle and directory publication tasks own authenticated connection and payload enforcement. Outcome and per-command/mutant logs use the task ID on the board.\\n\\n## 2026-09-07\\n\\n### 9ny4xl: R1–R6 closed — probe-availability claims corrected, marker census measures effect, catalog directive pinned\\n- SCOPE: TASK-260907-9ny4xl (story final leaf). `internal/cigate` claim tests + effect census + splitter tests + `doc.go`, `internal/catalog` directive pin, `.github/workflows/ci.yml` comments + freshness guard, README CI table + 20 probe notes, 2249 correction below. Leaves 1–5 production untouched; `claims.go` production changed only in comments; `catalog.go` production unchanged.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2845,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 712,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
